Package: zenos
Version: @VERSION@
Section: x11
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Maintainer: The ZENOS Authors <zenos-authors@users.noreply.invalid>
Depends: python3 (>= 3.11), ffmpeg, python3-gi, python3-gi-cairo, gir1.2-gtk-3.0, gir1.2-webkit2-4.1, gir1.2-gstreamer-1.0,
 gstreamer1.0-plugins-base, gstreamer1.0-plugins-good, gstreamer1.0-plugins-bad, gstreamer1.0-libav,
 python3-cryptography, python3-numpy, python3-opencv, python3-fonttools, python3-tk,
 nodejs (>= 24.22.1), kdialog, kde-cli-tools, inotify-tools, xdg-user-dirs, xdotool, x11-utils, iptables, pulseaudio-utils, unattended-upgrades,
 plasma-desktop, plasma-workspace, kwin-x11, fcitx5, fcitx5-anthy, fonts-inter, fonts-morisawa-bizud-gothic, bpftrace
Recommends: libreoffice-writer, libreoffice-calc, libreoffice-impress, sddm
Description: ZENOS desktop for classified work (Developer Preview)
 ZENOS turns a KDE Plasma desktop into a workstation for levelled, sealed files:
 files carry a security level, opening above your level goes through an approval
 request, and leak-like behaviour stops the session until officers release it.
 Includes the ZENOS browser, office, PDF, image and video apps, and ZENOS Messages.
 .
 This is a proof of concept and not yet safe for real classified data. See
 /usr/share/doc/zenos/THREAT_MODEL.md.
